sweet-touch-irq1 (lowclk 2026-11-14; design: docs/research/155-touch-ftm5-interrupt.md sections 3, 5, 6 "Stage 1"): FTM5 touch interrupt STAGE 1 behind boot-arg sweettouchirq=1: the touch thread waits on the gpa9[0] level-low EINT (GIC INTID 67 = SPI 35) instead of the 8 ms poll. Stage 0 (patch 0355, sweettouchirq=2) stays exactly as it is.
Sources [read]: research 155 with its citations; Linux v6.17 drivers/pinctrl/samsung/pinctrl-exynos.c (exynos_irq_mask :58-87 EMASK |= bit, exynos_irq_ack :89-110 EPEND := bit as a plain store, exynos_irq_unmask :112-152 level types ack first then EMASK &= ~bit, exynos_irq_set_type :154-210 ECON: con &= ~(EXYNOS_EINT_CON_MASK << shift); con |= trig << shift with shift = EXYNOS_EINT_CON_LEN * hwirq) and pinctrl-exynos.h (refs copy refs/wlan-stage1/linux-pinctrl-exynos.h:44-50: EXYNOS_EINT_LEVEL_LOW = 0, EXYNOS_EINT_CON_MASK = 0xF, EXYNOS_EINT_CON_LEN = 4; :20 EXYNOS_PIN_CON_FUNC_EINT = 0xf); gs101 pinctrl-gs.c:79 (gpa9: pad base 0xC0, eint_offset 0x18); gs101-pinctrl.dtsi:92-105 (gpa9 per-pin SPI 35, level high); fts_touch ftm5/fts.c:5303-5304 (the vendor driver requests level low, oneshot, threaded). ENCODING of ECON level low: the pin 0 field (bits [3:0], 4 bits per pin, mask 0xF) := EXYNOS_EINT_LEVEL_LOW = 0; the field is 4 bits wide in the source, so this patch writes the 4-bit nibble, not bits [2:0]. Hardware facts observed by stage 0 on the phone (boot 9ec5): ECON 0, EFLTCON 0, EMASK 0xff, EPEND 0, pad CON func 0, DAT idle 1, the line low while the FIFO holds events and high when empty (87689 of 87689 empty passes high).
sweettouchirq absent or 0 = behaviour unchanged byte for byte: no mapping, no register access, no GIC call, no log line, the poll loop unchanged (the only added statements that run are flag tests of tg_sti1.mode). sweettouchirq=2 = patch 0355's stage 0, unchanged. sweettouchirq=1 = stage 1 (stage-0 counters do not run). Any other value = `TOUCH GAP: sweettouchirq=%d: unknown value ...`, treated as 0 (0355's "stage 1 not in this patch" text is no longer reachable: the glue gives sti_arg only the value 2).
Arm (touch thread only, once, after the scan enable, after the controller-ready event of the existing reset path was seen, behind the existing AP-owns-the-bus mux check; the core refuses otherwise with a GAP and writes nothing): reads CON, DAT, ECON, EFLTCON, EMASK, EPEND and logs them; refuses (GAP, nothing written) if the pad CON func is not 0 or all four EINT words read 0xffffffff. Then, in this order, each a read-modify-write of pin 0's field with read-back: (a) EMASK bit 0 := 1; (b) CON [3:0] := 0xF; (c) ECON [3:0] := 0 (level low); (d) EPEND := 0x1 (W1C); then log DAT; (e) GIC attach INTID 67 DISABLED (patch 0346 sweet_spi_attach_off); (f) EMASK bit 0 := 0; (g) state ARMED, GIC enable (sweet_spi_enable; the enable bit must read back 1). Any failure tears down exactly the steps done and logs a GAP.
ISR (interrupt context): EMASK bit 0 := 1, EPEND := 0x1, publish the sequence number, thread_wakeup of the touch thread, return 0. No SPI access, no log call, no GIC call (the host test traps all three). A write failure or more than 1000 entries in one second: off_req, return 1 (the dispatcher masks the INTID), the thread disarms. An entry in any state other than ARMED (the line went low in the teardown gap before the mask store; review 0356 F1) does the same EMASK bit 0 := 1 store and returns 1, never 0 with the level still asserted. Thread (every pass): drain the FIFO as before; classify the pass by the sequence number (interrupt wake or safety-timeout drain); if the ISR ran since the last unmask: EPEND := 0x1, then EMASK bit 0 := 0 (Linux order), no read-back (the line may fire at once); a drain error (n < 0) is never followed by an unmask, and 10 drain errors in a row turn the mode off (review F2); after a successful unmask one DAT read: low with no interrupt entered since = counted (rechk_low) and one more drain at once (review F3). The wait while armed is assert_wait with a 100 ms safety timeout, re-checked against the sequence number before the block (no lost wakeup); the first drain after a wake is immediate. Not armed = today's loop exactly (1 ms with events, 8 ms idle).
Auto-off to polling, each with a GAP line (rule 7) and the summary row's reason: storm (more than 200 interrupt wakes with an empty FIFO in one second, or more than 1000 ISR entries in one second); line stuck low (DAT low after 3 empty drains in a row; research 155 U6: if DAT does not show the pad with CON = 0xF this trips and the log says so); no interrupt (10 safety-timeout drains in ONE 10 s window that found events although no interrupt came; the numbers 3, 10 and 1000 are GUESSES); any register read or write failure, refusal or read-back mismatch; GIC attach or enable failure; ISR error. Disarm order (every exit): EMASK bit 0 := 1, GIC detach, ECON back to the value read at arm, CON back to the value read at arm (0), EPEND := 0x1; every step is tried whatever failed before. Exits: auto-off (thread), clean stop (sweet_clean_stop calls sweet_touch_irq1_quiesce: no more arming, the touch thread disarms at its next pass, waits up to 500 ms), every OTHER reset path (sweet_machine_reset_x, second statement after the pets stop): sweet_touch_irq1_mask_off = lock-free, no print, no GIC call, the ONE write EMASK bit 0 := 1, and only if the line was ever unmasked.
Summary row every 10 s: `SWEET TOUCH IRQ: irqs N empty N wakes N tmo_drains N tmo_found N storm N mode irq|off:<why>`.
HARDWARE WRITES OF THIS PATCH [the only new ones; all in bsd/dev/sweet_touch_irq1.h through sti1_rmw, one allowlist sti1_rows[] + the value rules of sti1_wr_ok; the kernel store tg_sti1_wr in sweet_touch_gs101.c has a second, independent allowlist: offsets 0x0C0, 0x718, 0x918, 0xA18 and EPEND value 1 only]: CON 0x174D00C0 [3:0] := 0xF at arm / back to the arm-time value (0) at disarm; ECON 0x174D0718 [3:0] := 0 at arm / back to the arm-time value at disarm; EMASK 0x174D0918 bit 0 := 1 (arm, ISR, disarm, reset path) and := 0 (arm, thread after each ISR); EPEND 0x174D0A18 := 0x1 (arm, ISR, thread, disarm). Every RMW preserves the other seven pins' bits exactly (checked by the judge). NOT written: EFLTCON 0x174D0828 (read only), PUD 0x174D00C8, DRV, any other pin, the SPI/USI/CMU words, gpp23/gpp26. GIC: attach_off, enable, detach of INTID 67 through the patch 0346 helpers only. The EMASK word is shared by eight pins but written by nobody else in XNU; ISR and thread never write it at the same time by construction (header comment of sweet_touch_irq1.h).
Files: new bsd/dev/sweet_touch_irq1.h (pure core between STI1_CORE_BEGIN/END, host test tools/test_touch_irq1_core.py with a fake gpa9 bank, fake FTM5 and fake GIC), bsd/dev/sweet_touch_gs101.c (boot-arg, ops, ISR trampoline, sleep, arm and loop hooks, quiesce, reset hook), bsd/dev/sweet_restart.c (two calls). Needs patch 0346 (sweet_spi_attach_off/enable/detach) and 0355. Diffed against the k11 tree (0355 applied). ORDER: after 0355.
NOT RUN ON HARDWARE (the kernel glue is built but not host-run). The new write path is UNREVIEWED: it needs the rule-8 Opus review (AGENTS.md rule 8) before it boots. Unknowns that only the boot settles: whether DAT shows the pad with CON = 0xF (U6), whether EPEND latches a level that is still low (U4: the safety timeout covers it), whether the EINT window answers writes from XNU (U3 was read-only), the three GUESS thresholds.
